multiplexing  serial  communications  interface  For  6‐port BOCA
IOAT66 board: The  driver  provides  support  for  BOCA  Research
IOAT66  boards  that  multiplex together up to six communications
interfaces.  Each device is the master device for up to  six  de‐
vices.  The kernel configuration specifies these devices as slave
devices  of  the  device, as shown in the synopsis.  The slave ID
given for each device determines which bit in the interrupt  mul‐
tiplexing  register is tested to find interrupts for that device.
The specification for the device is used to compute the base  ad‐
dresses for the subdevices. The port for the interrupt multiplex‐
ing  register  is  not programmable.  The driver was adapted from
the boca driver by Michael Richardson.
